# WHY (2026-09-21): with `core.autocrlf=true` —the usual setting on Windows— a merge
# or a freshly created worktree left the WORKING COPY in CRLF even though the
# index was in LF. Two things broke because of it, and both looked like a code
# failure:
#   · the MUTANTS of `tests/test-orchestrator-control.mjs` look in the source
#     for a piece of text written with `\n`; in CRLF they did not find it and the
#     suite reported «mutant setup… exists as-is in the source», and it also
#     crashed at the end with an ENOENT;
#   · comparing `agents/` and `commands/` with the copies already installed
#     failed by ONE byte of difference per line.
# Measured on the source repo's `master` after merging T1+T2: 6 failures and a
# suite crash that do not exist in LF. With this the whole repo is stored and
# checked out in LF (on macOS this changes nothing; it keeps both systems equal).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
